The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

==Professional dancers==
On 21 June 2017, the list of professionals returning for the fifteenth series was revealed. Professionals from the last series who did not return included [[Joanne Clifton]], [[Natalie Lowe]], and [[Oksana Platero]]. They were replaced by former ''[[Dancing with the Stars (Australian season 15)|Dancing with the Stars Australia]]'' professional [[Dianne Buswell]], [[Nadiya Bychkova]], and [[Amy Dowden]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/a8f6012a-b783-4fdb-ac7b-a995ef2cb4b7|title=Three new sensational dancers join our professional dancer line up for 2017|date=21 June 2017|website=Strictly Come Dancing}}</ref> This series saw the final appearance of professional dancer [[Brendan Cole]].

==Couples==
In the fifteenth series, there were fifteen celebrity contestants. On 7 August 2017, the first celebrity announced to be participating in the series was [[The Saturdays]] singer [[Mollie King]].<ref name="King">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/6525d4c5-3e53-4546-b336-45ebae3cf879|title=Mollie King is our first celebrity of Strictly 2017!|date=7 August 2017|work=BBC News |access-date=7 August 2017}}</ref> Celebrity reveals continued through the month with the line-up fully announced on ''[[The One Show]]'' on 21 August 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/BBCTheOneShow/status/899677177888870401|title=We will be revealing the final three @bbcstrictly 2017 contestants live from 7&nbsp;pm. Any guesses who the final three might be?|date=21 August 2017|access-date=29 August 2017|website=Twitter}}</ref><ref name="Burke">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/entries/c27f955d-460b-4ce3-841a-9f4ed16c12e2|title=Popstar Alexandra Burke completes the Strictly 2017 line-up!|work=BBC News |date=21 August 2017|access-date=21 August 2017}}</ref>

